        "content": "<p>In the documentation for Linear Recurrences it is noted that a closed form for linear recurrences is not yet implemented, as \"we are waiting for definition and properties of eigenvalues and eigenvectors\". It seems eigenvalues and eigenvectors are now in mathlib. Is anyone currently working on getting this closed form?</p>",
        "id": 585884105,
        "sender_full_name": "Emil Rugaard Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776341815
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/3dcb7dd9c8523150fc723ed10e477dd0254b51b1/Mathlib/Algebra/LinearRecurrence.lean#L36-L37\">link</a>)</p>",
        "id": 585899721,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776345492
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We do have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearRecurrence.geom_sol_iff_root_charPoly#doc\">docs#LinearRecurrence.geom_sol_iff_root_charPoly</a><br>\nI tried to work on this a few months ago but I couldn't find good sources.<br>\nHere's the theorem statement I have locally:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- The sequence `n ↦ n^k * q^n` is a solution of `E` iff `q` is a root</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">of `E`'s characteristic polynomial with multiplicity larger than `k`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isSolution_pow_mul_pow_iff_lt_rootMultiplicity_charPoly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsSolution</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">charPoly</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rootMultiplicity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">charPoly</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lt_iff_add_one_le</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">le_rootMultiplicity_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
